From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: The Playport authors <dev@playport.dev>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 02:03:21 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] ntdll: make the process heap's first region
 HeapSegmentReserve, as Windows does

Wine creates the process heap with RtlCreateHeap( flags, NULL, 0, 0 ),
which makes its first region 64 KB; further regions come from
elsewhere as it grows. A block can then end exactly at the first
region's end, with no mapping after it.

RDR2 on the phone ended with 0xc0000005 right after PlayRDR2's
"Unable to launch game" box closed, in about one run in three (r1,
n1, a1): its main thread read a 12-character wide string at the
process heap's base + 0xffe8, one character past its end, at
base + 0x10000, which no Wine view covers. The read is the game's,
but on Windows the process heap's first segment is the PEB's
HeapSegmentReserve (1 MB by default), and inside such a region
Wine's heap keeps a free entry committed after the last block, so
a short over-read stays in mapped memory.

Create the process heap with the PEB's HeapSegmentReserve and
HeapSegmentCommit (1 MB and 64 KB unless the registry sets them).

Linear: PLA-413
Class: upstream-bug
Evidence: docs/evidence/2026-10-21-rdr2-cs-fastpath-and-heap.md
Offered-upstream: no
---
 dlls/ntdll/loader.c | 10 +++++++++-
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/dlls/ntdll/loader.c b/dlls/ntdll/loader.c
index 4c85161..adffb8a 100644
--- a/dlls/ntdll/loader.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/loader.c
@@ -5997,7 +5997,15 @@ void loader_init( CONTEXT *context, void **entry )
             heap_top_down_hack = TRUE;
         }
 
-        peb->ProcessHeap        = RtlCreateHeap( heap_flags, NULL, 0, 0, NULL, NULL );
+        /* Playport: the process heap's first region is HeapSegmentReserve (1 MB) with
+         * HeapSegmentCommit committed, as Windows makes it, not 64 KB. With 64 KB, a block
+         * could end exactly at the region's end, and a read just past it faulted: RDR2's
+         * main thread read a 12-character string at heap+0xffe8 one character past,
+         * at heap+0x10000, which Wine does not map (0xc0000005 right after PlayRDR2's
+         * box closes, runs r1, n1, a1). Inside a larger region the heap keeps a
+         * free entry committed after the last block. */
+        peb->ProcessHeap        = RtlCreateHeap( heap_flags, NULL, peb->HeapSegmentReserve,
+                                                 peb->HeapSegmentCommit, NULL, NULL );
 
         RtlInitializeBitMap( &tls_bitmap, peb->TlsBitmapBits, sizeof(peb->TlsBitmapBits) * 8 );
         RtlInitializeBitMap( &tls_expansion_bitmap, peb->TlsExpansionBitmapBits,
